From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 23:18:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 75/82] web-app: all-media gallery names the chat each webxdc
 app came from
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Apps tab of "All Media" mixes apps from every chat, and nothing in the
row said where an app came from — the only way to find out was the context
menu's "Show in chat".

Each row now carries its chat twice over: the chat avatar badged onto the
bottom-right corner of the app icon (same construction as the message search
results in the chat list — 20px avatar with a 1.6px outline in the surface
colour so it reads as a badge over the icon), and the chat name in front of
the app's own summary, separated by a middle dot. Apps mostly have an empty
summary, so the second line usually just reads as the chat name.

Only in the global gallery: `Gallery` passes `showChat` (chatId === 'all')
through the grid's itemData to the item component, and per-chat galleries
render exactly as before.

Three layout fixes the added text made necessary:

- The summary is now a single ellipsized line instead of wrapping into a
  second line that the fixed 61px row height clipped mid-sentence. The chat
  name comes first, so it is the app's own summary that gets cut.
- A `button` is shrink-to-fit, so with a non-wrapping summary the row grew
  past its grid cell and was clipped by the cell's overflow, i.e. cut
  mid-word with no ellipsis. The row now fills the cell (minus its margins),
  which also makes the hover background span the whole cell.
- `.text-part`'s max-width subtracted 37px for a 44px icon plus its 8px
  margin; with the row now exactly cell-width, the missing 15px pushed the
  text out of the cell. It subtracts 52px.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
